content.text:
Now main.js. Let me write carefully and completely.

Structure:

```js
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { ... } from ...
const SAVE_KEY = 'voxelcraft.save.v1';
const SEED_KEY = 'voxelcraft.seed.v1';

const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);

// error handler
window.addEventListener('error', ...)? display.

function readSave()...
function parseSeed...
```

URL params: `seed`, `fresh`.
On new world, use `location.replace(url)` with seed & fresh.

Init:
```
let renderer;
try { ... } catch(e) { show error; }
const canvas = $('game');
const scene = new THREE.Scene();
const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(75, aspect, 0.08, 900);
scene.add(camera);
```
Add camera to scene for held item? Using overlay scene, no need.

Atlas: buildAtlas(); atlasTexture = createAtlasTexture(THREE, atlasCanvas).

Materials.

UI callbacks defined with functions; instantiate UI after atlas.

Sky: new Sky(scene, renderer); sky.setFogDistance(settings.fog); set time from save if matching.

Particles.

Audio.

State:
```
const state = {
  mode:'menu', paused:false, inventory:false, ready:false,
  world:null, player:null, seed, save:null, target:null,
  mining:false, miningProgress:0, miningKey:'', mineSoundTimer:0,
  rightHeld:false, rightCooldown:0,
  heldItem:null, heldBlockId:null, swing:0, swingDir:0,
  pendingStart:false, startTime:0, lastSave:0, dirty:false,
  underwater:false, wasUnderwater:false,
  seedChanged:false, ...
}
```

Seed resolution:
```
const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
const fresh = params.has('fresh');
if (fresh) localStorage.removeItem(SAVE_KEY);
const save = readSave();
const urlSeed = parseInt(params.get('seed'));
const storedSeed = parseInt(localStorage.getItem(SEED_KEY));
let seed = Number.isFinite(urlSeed) ? urlSeed : (save?.seed ?? (Number.isFinite(storedSeed)?storedSeed:1337));
localStorage.setItem(SEED_KEY, String(seed));
const useSave = save && save.seed === seed && !fresh;
```
When fresh param, remove save. Could also clear URL param after? not needed.

Player state saved if useSave.

UI init after seed known; set seed field.

World build:
```
const worldApi = await buildWorld(seed, useSave?save.edits:null);
```
Need UI progress. Instantiate UI before world generation. The UI constructor calls onSettings which might reference world/sky; guard with optional.

Define callbacks referencing functions hoisted.

buildWorld:
```
async function buildWorld(seed, edits) {
  const world = new World(scene, {seed, chunks: 12, materials, edits});
  window.__world=world;
  await world.generate(p => ui.setGeneration(p, ...));
  state.world = world;
  particle system scene global existing.
  player = new Player(world, camera);
  if (savedPlayer) validate ...
  ui.setReady(`${size}×${size} · сід ${seed}`);
  state.ready=true;
  sky.setFogDistance(settings.fog);
  if (state.pendingStart) startGame();
}
```
Note particles created once before world.

Atlas textures: all good.

Cinematic:
```
let menuAngle=0;
function updateMenuCamera(dt){
 menuAngle += dt*0.05;
 const cam = camera;
 const h = state.ready ? 62 : 70;
 camera.position.set(Math.cos(menuAngle)*90, h, Math.sin(menuAngle)*90);
 camera.lookAt(0, 36, 0);
 if (camera.fov !== 55) {camera.fov=55; updateProjectionMatrix}
}
```
When ready and user clicks Play, reset fov 75.

Maybe cinematic should show island better: orbit radius 110, height 58, lookAt(0,34,0). Menus on left, view on right; good. Sky/clouds.

Render loop:
```
let lastTime=performance.now(); let frames=0, fpsTime=0, fps=0;
function animate(now){
 const dt = Math.min(0.1, (now-lastTime)/1000) || 0;
 lastTime=now;
 if (state.mode==='menu') updateMenuCamera(dt);
 else if (state.mode==='playing') {
   if (!state.paused && !state.inventory) { player.update(dt, world); updateInteraction(dt); }
   updateHeld(dt);
   targeting();
   ...
 }
 sky.update(dt, camera) except paused? keep sky moving even paused? time only advances if not paused. We can update sky always with dt (world time continues while paused) but day/night moving while paused is a nice touch. However menu time also advances. Fine.
 updateWaterMaterial(...);
 apply fog underwater...
 particles.update(dt) only if not paused? keep.
 update HUD.
 renderer.render(scene,camera);
 if playing render held overlay.
 requestAnimationFrame(animate);
}
```
Need sky.update before camera? uses camera position for sky sphere; set after player update. Good.

When menu, use camera cinematic; pause state doesn't update player.

FPS display every 0.5s.

Underwater:
```
if playing { const under = player.isUnderwater(); if (under !== state.underwater) { audio.splash?; ui.setUnderwater(under); state.underwater=under; }
 if under: sky.fog.color.set('#124b66'); sky.fog.near=0.1; sky.fog.far=26; else setFogDistance(settings.fog)
}
```
Do this after sky.update (which sets fog color horizon/near/far from setFogDistance). Note sky.setFogDistance stored fogFar; update doesn't reset near/far except at init/settings. Actually Sky.update doesn't reset near/far; only fog.color. So if underwater changes near/far, must restore after. Implement:
```
const far = state.underwater ? 26 : settings.fog;
sky.fog.near = state.underwater ? 0.5 : far*0.45;
sky.fog.far = far;
if underwater sky.fog.color.set('#124b66')
```
But sky.fog.color is set to horizon each update; override after. Water material uses fog color; good.

Clock: update UI every 0.5s with `sky.clockString`, night = sun elevation < 0.03.

Interaction:
- recompute target each frame (raycast 7). set selection mesh position.
- Mining progress:
```
if (mining && target && allowed) {
 key = `${x},${y},${z}`
 if key != state.mineKey reset
 const hardness = BLOCKS[id].hardness; state.miningProgress += dt / hardness;
 particles every 0.12
 if >=1 breakBlock(target)
} else decay (miningProgress -= dt*2, min 0)
ui.setBreakProgress(...)
```
Don't allow mining if paused/inventory.
- Breaking bedrock disallowed.
- If block is cross (plants), hardness .04 → almost instant.
- Break block: world.setBlock(x,y,z,AIR); if success: particles, audio; state.dirty = true; target=null.
  - Particle color computed from tile average map.
  - Also if water adjacent, water rebuild flagged.
  - Note world.setBlock records edits with AIR; save includes 0.
- Dig sound interval.
- Selection: if target && playing. For cross plants the box okay.

Place block:
```
function placeBlock() {
 const t = state.target; if (!t) return;
 const id = ui.selectedBlock;
 let px=t.x+t.normal[0]...
 if (!world.inBounds(px,pz) or py<1) return;
 const existing = world.getBlock(px,py,pz);
 if (existing !== AIR && existing !== WATER && !isCross(existing)) return;
 if (isSolid(id) && player.intersectsBlock(px,py,pz)) return; // don't place inside
 if (world.setBlock(px,py,pz,id)) { audio.place(BLOCKS[id].sound); particles; swing; dirty; }
}
```
Maybe placing over water should replace water; ok.

Swing on mine start and place. `state.swing = Math.min(1, state.swing + 1)`? Use animation timer `swingT` from 0..1; set to 0 on action, advance. Actually set `swingT = 1` and decay; rotation sin((1-swingT)*π). Implement:
```
state.swing = 1;
updateHeld: state.swing = max(0, state.swing - dt*3.2); swingPhase = 1-state.swing; rot = sin(phase*PI)*...
```
If swing becomes 0, no offset.

Held item creation:
```
const heldScene = new THREE.Scene();
const heldCamera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(50, aspect, 0.01, 10);
heldCamera.position.set(0,0,0);
heldScene.add(new HemisphereLight(0xffffff,0x445544,1.5));
const hl = new DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1.6); hl.position.set(0.6,1,0.7); heldScene.add(hl);
const heldRoot = new THREE.Group(); heldScene.add(heldRoot);
buildHeldItem(id)
```
Build block:
- remove children of heldRoot except arm? Create group `heldBlockGroup`; arm separate persistent.
- arm: BoxGeometry(0.16,0.5,0.16) skin; position (0.24,-0.52,-0.15); rotation (0.5,0,-0.35)? It's in camera space: x right, y up, z toward viewer positive; at z=-0.6. Arm from bottom right toward block. Set arm position (0.3,-0.55,-0.45), rotation x 0.7, z -0.25. Block at (0.45,-0.3,-0.75). Hmm camera FOV 50, at z 0.75 visible half-height ~0.35; holding block at x .45 is outside? Aspect 1.6: half-width at z .75 = tan(25°)*.75*1.6 ≈ 0.56, so x .35 visible. Set block (0.32,-0.26,-0.8), scale cube side 0.5? Big. Minecraft held block about 0.25 of screen height. Side 0.36. Position x 0.34, y -0.3. Screen: at z 0.8, visible half-height .37; block center y -0.3, bottom -0.48 clipped bottom; Minecraft hand at bottom-right partly clipped. Fine. Make group position (0.38,-0.4,-0.75), cube side 0.34 centered → extends y -0.57..-0.23; bottom clips. Looks like held item.

Use BoxGeometry(0.34). Rotation (0.15, -0.5, 0.08).

For block cube materials:
```
const geometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(1,1,1);
const mats = FACE_TILES.map(tile => {
  const tex = atlas.clone();
  tex.repeat.set(1/8,1/8);
  tex.offset.set((tile%8)/8, 1 - (Math.floor(tile/8)+1)/8);
  tex.needsUpdate = true;
  return new THREE.MeshLambertMaterial({map:tex, transparent: id===10||id===17});
});
```
BoxGeometry face order: +X, -X, +Y, -Y, +Z, -Z. Tiles: side, side, top, bottom, side, side.
Note texture flipY default true and offset; tile rows count from top? With flipY true, texture v=0 is bottom of image; offset.y = 1-(row+1)/8 for row from top? We want region rows; in UV space with flipY, top row of image corresponds v near 1. offset.y = 1 - (row+1)/8 indeed. Good.

For cross item: use two planes PlaneGeometry(0.34,0.34) with material map clone of tile (transparent alphaTest, DoubleSide), positioned cross, rotated. Use MeshLambertMaterial transparent? alphaTest 0.3 side DoubleSide. Fine.

Arm color skin #d6a077. Add a sleeve? Keep simple. Maybe better draw a "hand" skin box.

Held item overlay also shows selection change (rebuild). Keep `state.heldId`.

Update held item bob:
```
group.position.x = 0.38 + cos(bob)*0.012*bobAmount;
group.position.y = -0.4 + sin(bob*2)*0.015*bobAmount - swing*0.1;
group.rotation.x = 0.15 + sin(swingPhase*π)*0.7;
group.rotation.z = 0.08 + sin(...)*0.15;
```
Need base values.

Render held overlay:
```
renderer.autoClear = true; renderer.render(scene, camera);
if (playing && !paused? show held even paused? hide when menu) {
 renderer.autoClear = false; renderer.clearDepth(); renderer.render(heldScene, heldCamera);
}
```
renderer.autoClear default true; set false globally and manually clear? Simpler keep true for main render, then set autoClear=false for overlay and restore true. Each frame.

Targeting selection mesh:
Create BoxGeometry(1.005) EdgesGeometry; LineBasicMaterial({color:0x000000, transparent:true, opacity:0.45}); linewidth ignored. Also add subtle white outline? Black works on all. In dark caves invisible; okay. Maybe color 0xffffff with opacity .5 and depthTest false? White selection like Minecraft black outline. Use two boxes? Keep black with depthTest true and renderOrder 4.

When target none hide.

Raycast origin = player eye; direction = player.forwardVector. But camera may bob; use camera.getWorldDirection for accuracy. Use player.forwardVector.

Note player's eye/camera; use eyePosition.

Mouse input:

```
canvas.addEventListener('mousedown', e => {
 if (state.mode!=='playing' || state.paused || state.inventory) return;
 audio.enable();
 if (!isLocked) requestLock();
 if (e.button===0) { state.mining = true; }
 else if (e.button===2) { state.rightHeld=true; placeBlock(); state.rightCooldown=0.22; }
 else if (e.button===1) { pickBlock(); }
});
window.addEventListener('mouseup', e => { if(e.button===0) state.mining=false; if(e.button===2) state.rightHeld=false; });
```
Placement repeated in update if rightHeld && cooldown<=0.
Mining on mobile: state.mining true.

Mouse look:
```
document.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {
 if (state.mode!=='playing'||paused||inventory) return;
 if (document.pointerLockElement===canvas) player.look(e.movementX,e.movementY);
 else if (state.dragging) player.look(e.movementX,e.movementY);
});
```
Dragging fallback: set dragging on mousedown; on mouseup false. But left click mining both look drag and mine; acceptable. Might cause accidental look when clicking? no movement.

Pointer lock:
```
let lockPending=false;
function requestLock(){ try { canvas.requestPointerLock?.(); } catch{} }
document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', ()=>{
 if (document.pointerLockElement===canvas) { state.locked=true; }
 else { state.locked=false; if (state.mode==='playing' && !state.paused && !state.inventory && !state.suppressPause) pauseGame(); }
});
```
When we exit lock intentionally for pause/inventory, pauseGame sets paused first, so no double.

On startGame, request lock; in headless may throw no error.

Keyboard:
- state playing check; when in menu, Enter/Space? not.
- On pause/inventory/settings Esc handling.
- Prevent key repeat for F, E, Esc, digits.
- Movement flags only when playing and not paused/inv; keyup always clears.
- `KeyW` forward=1; ArrowUp; etc.
- Space jump true on keydown; on keyup false. Double space detection: if now-lastSpace<0.28 && !repeat → toggleFly; else lastSpace=now. But every jump press sets lastSpace; holding space gets repeat keydown ignored; double-tap works.
- Shift sprint true, also in fly descend (input.down) — currently sprint uses input.sprint only and input.down for sneak/descend. KeyShift sets sprint true AND down? On ground Shift should sprint (Minecraft), and sneak is Ctrl? I set down as sneak and fly descend. Better: Shift = sprint, Ctrl = sneak/descend. In UI hints say Shift біг. So keyShiftLeft → sprint true; keyControlLeft → down true. Mobile fly descending? Mobile fly button toggles; jump button ascends? We need descend button — none. Could make fly button while flying descend? Better add touch "fly" toggles and a small down? Our touch UI has jump and fly only; when flying, jump ascends and down requires... Add logic: while flying, long-press fly button descends? Simpler: in mobile, touching fly button toggles; descending by tapping fly? Hmm. Add a dedicated down arrow maybe. Could repurpose: when flying, jump button ascends; hold fly button toggles; no descend → stuck at altitude; can turn off fly to fall. Acceptable but not great. Add double function: touch fly button pointerdown toggles; while flying, "sneak" no. Add a small button under jump with down arrow? Touch actions currently 2 columns: left col fly & jump; right col place & mine. Add down button by changing t-jump? Let's add a fifth button "Униз" maybe in left col above fly; increases clutter. Alternatively in flight, tilt? no.
  Could make fly mode auto-hover and jump ascends, and tapping "fly" while flying toggles off; to descend, toggle off and fall. Acceptable.

- Inventory E; close with E/Esc.
- Digit keys 1-9.
- Wheel: if not overlays, select.
- F3 toggles showStats (checkbox update too).
- M mute.
- F toggles fly, show toast.

Pointer lock Escape: Browser exits pointer lock; our pointerlockchange pauses. Also keydown Escape may fire; guard if already paused.

Pause:
```
function pauseGame(){
 if (state.mode!=='playing') return;
 state.paused=true; state.mining=false; state.rightHeld=false;
 ui.showPause(); document.exitPointerLock?.();
 if (state.inventory) ui.hideInventory();
 saveGame();
}
function resumeGame(){
 state.paused=false; state.inventory=false; ...
 ui.hidePause();
 requestLock(); audio.ui();
}
```
If settings open and user presses Esc: close settings, stay paused.

Inventory:
```
function openInventory(){ if playing && !paused { state.inventory=true; state.mining=false; ui.showInventory(); document.exitPointerLock?.(); } }
function closeInventory(){ state.inventory=false; ui.hideInventory(); requestLock(); }
```
